   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to the qualifications of certain county probation officer directors",
    "basePrintNo": "S4757",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4757-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §257, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4757\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to the qualifications\nof certain county probation officer directors\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would allow the director of probation in counties with a\npopulation of more than three thousand to be appointed by the county\nexecutive with the approval of the local governing body.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 6 of section 257 of the\nexecutive law, as added by chapter 883 of the laws of 1983, to allow\nthe director of probation in counties with a population of more than\nthree hundred thousand, except counties wholly contained within a\ncity, to be in the non-competitive class of civil service and shall be\nappointed by the county executive with the approval of the local\ngoverning body, who shall be in the non-competitive class of civil\nservice Such deputy shall be appointed by the director of probation.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nCurrent law allows counties with a population of more than four\nthousand, except counties wholly contained within a city, to appoint\nthe director of probation with the approval of the local governing\nbody.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, all probation directors in counties of more than 400,000\nare appointments. This would allow counties with populations of more\nthan 300,000 to appoint the director of probation which will capture\nAlbany, Rockland and Orange counties.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
